# The devcontainer image is built with the repository root as its context and a
# Dockerfile that copies nothing out of it, so everything here is pure overhead
# -- and .pixi is worse than overhead. It holds the solved environment, half a
# gigabyte of it, including symlinks that the context hasher refuses outright:
#
#   failed to compute context hash: read .pixi/envs/default/lib/icu/current: is a directory
#
# So on any checkout where the environment has been installed -- which is every
# checkout the tests have ever been run in -- building the container failed
# before it started. The environment inside the container comes from a volume
# mount and pixi.lock, never from here.
.pixi/

# Local state with the same story: never copied, and only ever slows the build.
.git/
.pytest_cache/
